mireille: quick report 2 reproducible goroutine leak when a Generator.Stream is canceled while a background auth token refresher is rotating credentials. repro below. :bug:

mireille: ```go
func repro() {
  ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
  client := redwood.NewClient(tokenProvider.Current())
  gen := client.Generator("gpt-mini").Stream(ctx, Prompt("hello"))

  go func() {
    time.Sleep(50 * time.Millisecond)
    cancel()
  }()

  go func() {
    for {
      time.Sleep(120 * time.Millisecond)
      tokenProvider.Rotate()
      client.AuthRefresh()
    }
  }()

  for _ = range gen {
  }
}
```

raj: stack traces?

mireille: dump shows multiple goroutines in handshake/retry stuck on net/http transport dial even after ctx cancel. looks like some code paths don't observe the stream-level cancel.

michael: generator iterator lacks Close(); we rely on ctx cancel which races with auth refresh. python SDK has aclose(); maybe we need Close() in go too.

sofia: short term add Close() + doc. long term make handshake use per-stream derived ctx that is canceled when iterator is closed.

emily: agree. also add a unit test that simulates rotation + cancel and checks goroutine counts.

mireille: i'll push a failing test + small patch that cancels per-handshake contexts. will include example usage showing Close().

ci-bot: created draft PR mireille/stream-leak-fix (WIP)

raj: thanks 9 will review. we should also instrument active stream handles metric for support.

mireille: added metric in the patch. emily offered to update the sampleapp once PR lands. :thumbsup:
